    <summary>Gecko-first privacy browser with 101 JS anti-fingerprinting protections</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
# BearBrowser

A Gecko-first (Firefox ESR) privacy browser hardened against fingerprinting and tracking.

## Features

- **Gecko engine (Firefox ESR)** — rides FF140 ESR cohort for fingerprinting crowd anonymity
- **101 JS fingerprinting protections** — Canvas, WebGL, AudioContext, Fonts, Timing, WebRTC all spoofed or normalized
- **OS spoof layer** — reports normalized platform to avoid cross-session tracking
- **Anti-tracking** — uBlock-equivalent content filtering baked in, not as extension
- **SourceOS sovereign** — no Google sync, no telemetry, no cloud dependency
- **Windows native** — full Win32 browser integration, pinnable to taskbar
- **Automatic updates** — via Chocolatey or built-in update check

## Privacy Model

BearBrowser's fingerprinting shield operates at 101 distinct surfaces:
- Canvas 2D + WebGL pixel data randomization
- AudioContext frequency response spoofing
- Font enumeration normalization (reports common set)
- Screen resolution + color depth normalization
- Timezone offset stabilization
- Navigator property normalization
- Hardware concurrency normalization
- Battery status API disabled
- WebRTC leak prevention
- Sensor API disabled

## Windows Notes

On Windows, BearBrowser uses the Gecko engine exclusively (WKWebView is macOS-only).
The browser registers itself as a default browser option in Windows settings.
